From b7f65fb85390af3f57a324c9e8bfbfb0501219a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:47:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: type wallet load, encryption and rescan diagnostics

Migrate 21 related wallet startup/lifecycle callers. Preserve Info, wallet
prefixes, millisecond padding and six-place progress rendering. Versions,
key/record counts, derivation iterations, raw rescan block ID, height and
elapsed time remain typed. Names and bracketed display labels are separate.
No passphrase, seed, key contents or database payload is newly logged.
Wallet loading, encryption, scan decisions and release behavior are unchanged.
Shared eCash wallet tier, before V2 wallet adaptations.

Reuse the existing wallet caller adapter and its single cumulative catalog;
no new per-group tooling or tests. The WITH_LOCK expression in
CWallet::RescanFromTime remains unchanged because ast-grep reports a parse
error inside that macro; the mixed walletdb strErr paragraph also remains
for contextual treatment rather than pretending it has typed internals.

Scripted-diff commands (ast-grep-py==0.51.0):
  /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/wallet_callers.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/wallet-keypool-callers.json --report /private/tmp/wallet-startup-source-proof.json --apply
  git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/wallet/wallet.cpp src/wallet/walletdb.cpp src/wallet/wallettool.cpp

Reviewed source diff, existing exact-message/severity validator, cumulative
idempotent replay, typed-event lint (23 sites in these files), and
git diff --check pass. SOURCE ONLY: NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN; one combined
native build and focused controls are deferred until resource scheduling.
